---
import Tool from '../../layouts/Tool.astro';
import CcMap from '../../components/CcMap.astro';
---

<Tool slug="cc" wide shortcuts={[["← → ↑ ↓", "Move through the grid (when it has focus)"], ["Home / End", "CC 0 or CC 127"]]} description="All 128 MIDI Control Change numbers: what MIDI 1.0, GM and GM2 say, how synths use them, and the bytes to send. Move a knob on your controller to find its CC.">
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    What every Control Change number means: the MIDI 1.0 assignment, what General MIDI and GM2 require, and how
    synths commonly use it. Pick a controller to get its bytes on any channel, send it to a device, or connect a
    controller and move a knob to see which CC it sends.
  </Fragment>
  <CcMap />
  <p slot="after" class="note-small">
    “In practice” notes describe widespread conventions, not rules; check your instrument's MIDI implementation chart.
    For hardware synths, the community-maintained <a href="https://midi.guide/">MIDI Guide</a> collects CC and NRPN
    charts for hundreds of devices.
  </p>
</Tool>
